    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "DC-9-15\nEmergency\nProcedures\nSouthern\nPlease do not\nremove this card\nfrom the aircraft",
      "Overwater\nEmergency\nEquipment\nOn those flight segments involving ex-\ntended\noverwater\noperation\nyour\nDC-9-15 is equipped with all necessary\nemergency equipment.\nLife rafts are located in overhead racks\nforward and midway in the cabin of the\nDC-9 (see illustration). Sufficient life\nrafts are carried to accommodate all\npassengers and crew.\nA life preserver for each passenger is\nlocated directly beneath his seat. Please\nstudy the illustrations below for the\ncorrect method of donning and\noperating your life preserver.\nLife Raft\nLocations\nLife Preserver Operation\nPlace life preserver\nover head and pull\nstraps until back flap\nis fully extended.\nSecure \"D\" rings\nto front snap-hooks\nand pull tabs in an\noutward motion.\nForm 0-72\nAfter leaving aircraft,\ninflate by pulling\ndown sharply on\nthe two plastic tabs.\n(12-19-74)\nIf dark, pull\ncenter tab to\nactivate light\n2002.127.546"
    ],
